title ALES149 — Lotus's stereo_split_silence: the auto-splitter carried into stereo, one cut line for both channels, the stereo twin of the silence stripper, bound to ALES148 by the join law
prompt Read REMEMBER and the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think Recur lap. Read the 1024-round itinerary and the six-season double-seat; REMEMBER is 337KB with a giant living-edge line, so the true living edge is git: Season C, the Lotus creative suite (waymark ALES), last landed ALES148 stereo_trim_silence. Its own recommend named the ascending crux plainly: ALES97 (split_silence, the auto-splitter — cut AT the silence keeping each non-silent region as its own take) carried into stereo, the join-law twin of the trimmer just landed. Crux-first and Lindy-first agree — the stereo edit corner grows on the analysis readers, and the splitter is the trimmer's natural companion.
think Studied the just-completed pair: stereo_trim_silence (ALES148, the frame-walk with two monotonic per-channel cursors marking jointly-silent frames) and mono split_silence (ALES97, the Take/take_clip/coalesce shape). The stereo split fuses the two: ALES148's silence-intersection frame walk to decide jointly-silent per frame, ALES97's coalesce-into-takes shape at the frame level. A stereo take is a maximal span of consecutive NOT-jointly-silent frames, a shared span into both channels so every take is balanced by construction.
think The wall is the same one ALES148 named: splitting each channel by its own silence would cut the two speakers at different positions and tear every take apart, because ALES147 proved the two channels segment independently. So the rung decides one cut line for both — split only at jointly-silent frames, keep every frame either speaker fills. The honest binding is the JOIN LAW: re-joining the splitter's pieces per channel returns exactly ALES148's trimmed master byte for byte, binding ALES149 to ALES148 the way ALES97 is bound to ALES96.
think Implementation: split_stereo_on_silence takes a *const StereoClip (read-only — segment_stereo already takes *const, so no @constCast), segments both channels up front through ALES147 (all validation, empty-clip BadFrame → out left empty), then one forward pass advances a cursor per channel across its tiling run list, decides each frame jointly-silent, and coalesces not-jointly-silent frames into shared StereoTakes (max_stereo_takes = segment.max_segments, TakesFull named-honest); stereo_take_clip copies both channels' samples over the shared span through ALES2 splice into a fresh balanced destination, asserting empty-in and balanced-out. The stereo take law is proven against a second independent by-hand reference (frame verdicts by run scan, coalesced by hand) across eight frame lengths, four floors, three splits.
obs No custody gate reached — purely local, two bounded i16 Clips, a self-approved design round. First-try witness GREEN, no red this round (the @constCast instinct was caught and removed before building — segment_stereo's *const first param made it unnecessary). Recorded lesson: when a mono edit is READ-ONLY and produces a bounded result list (split → takes), the stereo lift is not run-mono-twice either — it composes the two independent reads into one shared cut line (the same intersection ALES148 proved), so the takes stay balanced and the join law binds it to the trimmer. Witness GREEN (four laws: take, join, preservation, degenerate/atomicity), tame_style_check bans clean, my module carries dense asserts (not on the zero-assert ratchet). Front door lotus/README.md synced (ALES149 roster entry, stamp 20260815.052853).
loom witness=ales_stereo_split_silence_witness result=GREEN laws=4 channels=2 class=stereo-edit read=reads-only+writes-fresh form=coalesce-into-takes decision=silence-intersection cases=stereo-take-law(8flen*4floor*3split)+join-law(rejoin=ALES148-trim-byte-for-byte)+preservation(left-silent-right-loud-kept-in-take)+degenerate(all-joint-silent-zero-takes,no-joint-silent-one-whole-take)+atomicity(empty,ragged,inverted-band,illegal-floor) reds=0
